# A head, and the point is that it *is* a machine.
#
# Experiment 13, note 1: a mine that produced ore because the catalogue said so
# was the last magical object left in the world. Now the room has a water table in
# the ground and this is what stands on it. It lifts 800 a second because
# a fluid inlet moves two hundred, an outlet takes two hundred, and they pair off, not because anybody typed a number.
#
# The ground has the last word: a head on a thinner seam turns slower, and a
# richer one takes more than one head -- or one better head, which is the same
# question asked of the floor instead. Everything here abuts everything else on
# purpose, because in a room whose problem is space the size of this is the
# first thing worth arguing with.

machine "Intake"

pump   W1 at 0,0
pump   W2 at 0,2
pump   W3 at 2,0
pump   W4 at 2,2

outlet O1 at 4,0
outlet O2 at 4,2
outlet O3 at 6,0
outlet O4 at 6,2

wire W1.water -> O1.liquid
wire W2.water -> O2.liquid
wire W3.water -> O3.liquid
wire W4.water -> O4.liquid
